<!-- outbound-fact-sourcing -->
**Memory is the first source for any fact that will leave this desk inside a
message.** Not only facts about a person or a company — also the codes and
number formats we tell people to use, prices, plan limits, what a step of a
procedure actually is, and what the product can and cannot do. Anything a reader
will act on. The read path is `cs ask`, which only reads.

The order is **engine memory, then past sent mail for precedent, then the
written project dossier (`cs project show`).** Memory is usually broader than any single place the
same fact also happens to be written down. To read the precedent behind a fact,
and the wording we used:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m cs rpc emails.search '{"query":"<terms>","folder":"sent","limit":8}'
.venv/bin/python -m cs rpc emails.list_by_thread '{"thread_id":"<id>"}'
```

**Repository source code is never a source for a customer-facing fact.** A file
in a codebase describes one implementation of one surface. It is routinely
narrower than what we know and tell people, and from the inside it gives no sign
that it is. Reading it and inferring the answer produces something that looks
sourced and is not.

**An empty search obliges a second source, never a derivation.** When one source
comes back with nothing, the next step is another source — never rebuilding the
fact out of whatever artifact happens to be nearby. When every source comes back
empty, that is the answer: say we do not have it, or put the question to the
operator. An unanswered question costs a round trip; an invented one is sent to
a customer over this company's name.

**A nonzero exit is not an empty search.** For `cs ask` and `cs chat`, an
engine-turn failure is reported on stderr; try another authorized source and
report the failed layer rather than asserting no facts were found.

`cs draft-reply` can save an engine draft before generation transport or
publication fails. Read its structured outcome even on nonzero exit; retain the
full saved draft ID, operation ID, achieved stages and uncertainty. Engine-saved
is not Gmail-visible. Resume an existing saved draft through the interactive
`cs-customer` procedure without generating another reply. Unknown publication or
send outcomes require exact operation reconciliation, never blind retry.
Scheduled workflows retain their holds and must never select `--operator-request`
or adopt an interactive recovery route to bypass their admission rules.
